.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt RE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm re
.Nd open a file in the running rook
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is
.Ql rook edit :
the same binary as
.Xr rook 1 ,
installed as a symlink and dispatching on
.Ql argv[0] .
It connects to the control socket of the running rook and asks it to open
.Ar file
in the editor, then exits.
It is a client, not an editor \(em without a running rook it fails with
.Ql no app listening on <sock> (is rook running?) .
.Pp
Exactly one
.Ar file
is read; extra arguments are ignored.
A relative path is resolved against the caller's working directory, so
.Nm
works from any pane, any directory.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ROOK_SOCK
.It Ev ROOK_SOCK
Socket to connect to.
Default
.Pa /tmp/rook.sock .
Shells inside a sandboxed instance
.Pq Ql rook --config=DIR
inherit that instance's value, so
.Nm
reaches the rook it was typed in.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Failure means no instance was listening, the path could not be resolved,
or the app refused the open
.Pq its reason is printed .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rook 1 ,
.Xr rook-ctl 7
